diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 2d526a2..8150b07 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -51,9 +51,109 @@ cd /workspace/ros2_ws
 source install/setup.bash
 
 ros2 launch storm_pick_place_demo pick_place_real.launch.py \
-  enable_motion:=true with_rviz:=true
+  robot_ip:=172.17.1.2 arm_id:=fer enable_motion:=true with_rviz:=true
 ```
 
+The established launch default remains `storm_task_file:=franka_reacher.yml`.
+Select the experimental port explicitly with
+`storm_task_file:=franka_reacher_cat_real.yml`.
+
+For live COSMIK in domain 29 on this workspace's local monitor:
+
+```bash
+ROS_DOMAIN_ID=29 DISPLAY=:1 ros2 launch storm_pick_place_demo pick_place_real.launch.py \
+  robot_ip:=172.17.1.2 arm_id:=fer enable_motion:=true with_rviz:=true \
+  storm_task_file:=franka_reacher_cat_real.yml
+```
+
+The real launch publishes an identity static transform `fer_link0` → `world`
+(or `<arm_id>_link0` → `world` for another arm ID), preserving the robot's existing
+`base` → `fer_link0` parent. This demo assumes COSMIK's world origin
+and axes coincide with the robot base; marker coordinates are used without an
+offset or rotation. The transform connects the human frames and robot frames
+for both RViz and the planner. `ROS_DOMAIN_ID` must be set when starting each
+process. The launch inherits it rather than changing the domain itself.
+
+The CaT profile uses native acceleration CaT
+with the corrected `paper` equations, seeded
+antithetic spline samples, fused inverse dynamics, explicit FER self-collision,
+and exact integration of the planner's latency prediction. The existing task
+manager still alternates the configured A/B targets; COSMIK markers still enter
+the native dynamic collision cost. Gripper phases and control gains are unchanged.
+
+For the reaching demo, `pick_place_task_manager_params.yaml` accepts arrival
+within 6 cm (and the existing 2 rad orientation tolerance), or switches to the
+other target after `target_timeout_sec: 10.0`. The timer starts when a valid
+target goal is available and spans all phases at that physical target; changing
+phase or swapping pick/place roles at the same pose does not reset it. A gripper
+action already in progress finishes before switching. Timeout events appear as
+`[task-event] target-timeout(...)` in the task log. Set `target_timeout_sec: 0.0`
+to disable timed alternation. The separate `phase_timeout_sec` retains its abort
+behavior and remains disabled here. Restart the demo to load these settings.
+
+The profile uses the existing FER model with inertias, closed-gripper collision
+coverage and SRDF exclusions, packaged under
+`/workspace/storm/content/assets/robot/fer_real`. It limits sampled acceleration
+to 5 rad/s² and considers 40% of URDF velocity limits and 80% of effort limits.
+The human clearance cost threshold remains 10 cm; explicit self-clearance is
+1 cm. These are planning constraints, not hard bounds on measured motion or
+the feedback torque. The model matches the current task's two zero gripper widths.
+All four CaT hazards use `p_max=0.15`: `p_max=1` lost its reward signal when all
+rollouts started inside a margin on the recorded moving-human example.
+The real launch applies a 0.1 rad reference inset for this CaT profile, removes
+outward velocity/acceleration at the inset, and feeds the projected reference
+back into the native integrator. Disarmed holds keep their measured position.
+
+For a comparison with the previous controller, append
+`storm_task_file:=franka_reacher.yml` to the same launch command. The original
+profile and the simulation launch remain available. No gain or temperature
+tuning from the exploratory benchmark has been promoted to this profile.
+
+Run the controller checks offline before a robot trial (these start no ROS nodes):
+
+```bash
+source /opt/ros/humble/setup.bash
+source /workspace/ros2_ws/install/setup.bash
+python3 /workspace/storm/scripts/validate_native_sampling_dynamics.py --compiled
+python3 /workspace/storm/scripts/validate_real_cat_profile.py --device cuda:0
+python3 /workspace/storm/scripts/validate_real_reference_guard.py
+python3 /workspace/storm/scripts/validate_cat_bag_replay.py --device cuda:0
+```
+
+The checks exercise the native rollout, moving obstacle updates, enabled CaT
+hazards, model/frame mapping and target alternation. They report compute times;
+they do not establish physical tracking or that this candidate has the best
+avoidance behavior. Compare reaching completion, human clearance, torque and
+jerk with the baseline on the robot using the same task and human stream.
+
+### Robot validation on 2026-10-02
+
+The port is **not yet validated for continuous human avoidance**. The actual
+arm completed A→B→A without human replay, at 10.90, 21.95 and 27.90 seconds from
+trial start, within the existing 25 mm target tolerance. About nine seconds of
+the first interval were optimizer startup/compilation. The command and task
+disarm acknowledgements succeeded.
+
+The 18-second COSMIK clip completed A and B in an ideal offline acceleration
+plant, with minimum modeled human clearance 29.2 mm and self-clearance 16.4 mm.
+The modeled pole clearance fell to 1.2 mm. These results omit physical tracking,
+state-filter behavior, asynchronous planning and startup time.
+
+Physical replay failed first with `joint_position_limits_violation` on joint 7.
+After correcting the position-only output clamp, a repeating replay reached A
+and B with at least 0.097 rad measured joint margin, then stopped on
+`self_collision_avoidance_violation` during the return toward A. That posture
+still had 74 mm clearance in the SRDF-filtered sphere model. Measured postures
+also overlapped replayed human capsules by up to 73 mm. The collision model,
+planner state/latency handling and CaT weighting need further work before this
+can be called a successful human-avoidance deployment. Raising hazard
+probabilities and self margin alone failed the offline replay and was rejected.
+
+Results and commands are in `validation/real_test/README.md`; measured telemetry,
+geometry checks, launch logs and a ROS bag of the corrected trial are beside it.
+RViz failed to open on this workspace's current X display; the controller stack
+and physical trials ran. Use `with_rviz:=false` here when a display is unavailable.
+
 ## Key Topics
 
 - Input state: `sensor` (`linear_feedback_controller_msgs/Sensor`)
